  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0 (branch cut from upstream/main f490458a).\n\n## What changed\n\n`Planner::step_search` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/grow.rs`): when no growth step holds the load, the fallback used to pick the least overload from the tries' readings. Those readings stop at the first point past the bound (`walk_until`). Where the overload comes before the step-dependent front, every try reads the same, the first and largest step wins the tie, and that step is then walked whole far past the reading it was picked on (#7 round 10, island NE corner: picked at 59.5 deg, cut at 125 deg).\n\nNow the fallback keeps each overloaded try's ring and revolution, but drops its partial stock. `least_whole` walks each revolution whole again from the planner's stock, largest step first. A smaller step replaces the kept one only when its whole reading is more than 2 % lower (`SLACK`, the tie tolerance the old fallback already used). Each re-walk stops early once it can no longer win. The kept revolution reuses the stock and reading from its whole walk, so it is not walked a third time.\n\n**#13 growth budget:** the re-walks are not charged as growth work, and `WORK_MAX`, `GEOM_MAX` and `GEOM_LEN` are unchanged. Each trial already charges its revolution's whole length (`add_len`) before its walk is cut short. The re-walk adds no new revolution and rebuilds no geometry: it reads revolutions already paid for in full, at most once each and usually only part way. The held fix e4039ef0 called the trial again instead, which rebuilt the offsets and charged length and vertices a second time; that is part of why its island run reached 61,971 r. The full reasoning is in `docs/decisions/845-adaptive-overload-fallback.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\nRelease `hsm_one` over all six `adaptive_hsm` fixtures, run with this fix and with upstream's `grow.rs`:\n\n| fixture | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| bore R12.5, rectangle 60x40, L-pocket, narrow slot 14x60, channel 22x60 | - | identical report lines (max deg, breaks, cut/air lengths, move counts, notes) |\n| island 60x40, 12x12 | HSM refused by law 3 after 109 revolutions (~600.0 k vertices, ~9.4 k r); Offset rings | HSM refused by law 3 after 118 revolutions (~606.4 k vertices, ~9.5 k r); Offset rings - identical posted path |\n\nOn the island, the smaller steps now kept in the overloaded corners mean more revolutions before the existing geometry law refuses the plan (118 instead of 109). The refusal and the Offset-rings path it falls back to do not change. No other fixture's output moves.\n\n**Goldens moved: none.** No committed CL/NC golden comes from the adaptive planner (`crates/app/tests/golden/` has no HSM/adaptive file), and no snapshot PNG is touched.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning test: `machining2d::adaptive::grow::tests::the_overload_fallback_keeps_the_least_whole_reading_not_a_truncated_tie` (camcraft-motion lib). Two overloaded revolutions share a 3 mm side-cut start past the bound. Walked to the bound, their readings are exactly equal (the old tie, which the larger step won). Walked whole, the larger step turns into fresh stock and reads much more, so the test asserts the smaller step is kept with its whole reading. Plus `a_near_tie_keeps_the_larger_step_and_nothing_tried_keeps_nothing`.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: motion lib + adaptive_band + adaptive_hsm + pocket3d_hsm, all green (33 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Release heavy lanes: `adaptive_hsm --ignored` (full-resolution report, island refused in seconds, channel trochoid fallback, small-helix rectangle) and the lib's `budget::fixtures::the_fixtures_that_grow_today_stay_under_the_geometry_budget`: green.\n- Debug camcraft-app adaptive suites (pocket3d_hsm, roughing2d, shoulder_adaptive, pocket_overhead, whole_model_pocket): all green (18 passed; 1 was already ignored).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The island fixture with the budget lifted (the issue's evidence run): the island is still refused by law 3 before its NE corner is grown, so the 125 deg corner overload no longer shows up in any posted path on main. The pinning test covers the mechanism directly.\n- The batch and release tiers.\n\nChangelog: Adaptive clearing's growth spiral, where no step holds the load, now cuts the step whose whole revolution overloads least, not the largest step on a tie read before the overload (#845)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #845\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
